{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GHmTmw5CQ7arSQAUm4nC5B","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Review rules for Kestrel\n2\t\n3\tEvery change gets three passes. Report each finding once, under the pass that found it.\n4\t\n5\t## Bugs\n6\t\n7\t- Does the code do what it claims? Check error paths: if the disable update fails, the bike must not stay rentable.\n8\t- The 48 hour deadline starts at the wrench `reported_at`, not when dispatch opens the job (SLA-4).\n9\t- Sorting or filtering must not drop open jobs. Feed field names follow GBFS v3 (`is_disabled`, `num_vehicles_disabled`).\n10\t\n11\t## Security\n12\t\n13\t- Validate every input on public routes in `src/server.ts`, such as `POST /wrench` and `GET /crew/queue`.\n14\t- Use bound parameters for SQL. No secrets in code or logs.\n15\t\n16\t## Compliance\n17\t\n18\t- Check the change against `work/spec.md` (AC-1 to AC-4) and `work/plan.md` (P-1 to P-3). Flag work no item asks for.\n19\t- Check `data/contract/sla.yaml`: SLA-4 (48 h wrenched), SLA-12 (feed accurate, at most 60 seconds old).\n20\t- No edits to `data/contract/` or approved `test/acceptance/` files. One commit per plan item, under 200 lines.\n21\t\n22\t## What Important means here\n23\t\n24\tA finding is Important only when riders, crews or the city contract would feel it. Example: a wrenched bike still shows `is_disabled: false` after 60 seconds, so a rider rents a broken bike and SLA-12 is breached.\n25\t\n26\t## Nits\n27\t\n28\tAt most 3 nits per review. Pick the ones that matter most and drop the rest.\n29\t\n30\t## Do not report\n31\t\n32\t- Anything in `data/` (recorded data, not code), and formatting.\n33\t\n34\t## How to write a finding\n35\t\n36\tOne table row per finding. Severity is Important or Nit.\n37\t\n38\t| Pass | Severity | Where | What goes wrong | Criterion |\n39\t| ---- | -------- | ----- | --------------- | --------- |\n40\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01CCPeEj4kziQq3XmRdFXL9G","agent_