{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015fYLD32yYDeQPnDXZ8Zigo","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Spec: wrench disables the bike, and the queue sorts by deadline\n2\t\n3\tFrom the approved `work/intent.md`. Claude Code interviewed the product manager, then wrote this spec.\n4\t\n5\t## Acceptance criteria\n6\t\n7\t- **AC-1**\n8\t  - WHEN a rider sends `POST /wrench` for a bike\n9\t  - THEN `vehicle_status.json` shows that bike with `is_disabled: true` within 60 seconds\n10\t- **AC-2**\n11\t  - WHEN a rider wrenches a bike at a station\n12\t  - THEN `station_status.json` shows `num_vehicles_disabled` for that station up by 1 within 60 seconds\n13\t- **AC-3**\n14\t  - WHEN a crew asks for `GET /crew/queue?depot=North`\n15\t  - THEN the jobs come back ordered by `deadline`, the job due first on top\n16\t- **AC-4**\n17\t  - WHEN a job comes from a wrench\n18\t  - THEN its `deadline` is 48 hours after the wrench `reported_at`, because the clock starts at the wrench\n19\t\n20\t## Concerns\n21\t\n22\t- Operations asked for a 15 minute grace period before a wrenched bike leaves the feed. SLA-12 in the contract says the feed is accurate \"at all times\". A grace period breaks that clause, so this spec does not include it. Owner: the product manager takes it to the city.\n23\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01CCPeEj4kziQq3XmRdFXL9G","agent_id":"aa975737ae9885ba7","session_id":"2224f79c-2ab4-4cc9-a55e-515fbe1ee521","uuid":"ab61d627-c01e-4efd-be3d-aa43cef509af","timestamp":"2026-11-13T05:23:16.490Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_015fYLD32yYDeQPnDXZ8Zigo","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"reviewer","task_description":"Review local-deadlines branch"}
